         recommended test: The change includes a test that checks the verdict call's defect payload is bounded by the configured obligation count.
           inputs:  Use a discrimination case with more obligations than the configured defect-verdict batch size, and make the verdict stage receive multiple defects per obligation so a defect-count-based bug would change how many obligations are packed into each verdict request. The input should include at least one batch where obligations have uneven defect counts, so counting defects instead of obligations produces a different request shape.
           detects: The verdict request could be built from the wrong batch dimension, so the number of defects carried per call would be bounded by the number of obligations instead of the configured defect-verdict batch size.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-verdict-call-carries-configured-bounded-obligations

