         recommended test: The change includes a test that edits one mapped test and observes another obligation's enumerated defects remain unchanged.
           inputs:  Run the enumeration step twice on the same obligations and changed code, but alter only one mapped test between runs. Choose at least two obligations with mapped tests so one can be edited while the other remains untouched. The edited test should be one whose name, inputs, or assertions would tempt a buggy implementation to leak mapping-derived data into another obligation’s enumeration request.
           detects: Editing one mapped test would leak into the enumeration request for a different obligation, so that other obligation's named defects would change even though its own mapping was untouched.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion test-editing-mapped-test-leaves-other-obligation-defects-unchanged

